WEBVTT

00:08:20.111 --> 00:08:22.467
- Any sign of it?
- Nothing.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.208
Are you sure this is bela's room?

00:08:26.302 --> 00:08:27.570
I'd say so.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.540
Dean?

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.439
Sweetie, are you there?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:47.639
Where are you?

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:49.340
Two states away by now.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.801
- Where?
- Where's our usual quippy banter? I miss it.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.585
I want it back, bela... now.

00:08:53.594 --> 00:08:57.056
Your little pistol, you mean?
Sorry. I can't at the moment.

00:08:57.057 --> 00:08:59.274
You understand how many
people are gonna die if you do this?

00:08:59.275 --> 00:09:01.660
What exactly is it that
you think i plan to do with it?

00:09:01.661 --> 00:09:05.999
Take the only weapon we have against an
army of demons and sell it to the highest bidder.

00:09:06.844 --> 00:09:09.578
- You know nothing about me.
- I know i'm gonna stop you.

00:09:09.579 --> 00:09:11.839
Tough words for a guy
who can't even find me.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.253
Oh, i'll find you, sweetheart.
You know why?

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:16.940
Because i have absolutely
nothing better to do

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:20.036
- Than to track you down.
- That's where you're wrong.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.339
You're about to be quite occupied.

00:09:22.858 --> 00:09:25.402
Did you really think
i wouldn't take precautions?

00:09:26.623 --> 00:09:28.040
Hands in the air!

00:09:33.635 --> 00:09:36.772
- That bitch!
- Turn around! Now!

00:09:38.573 --> 00:09:41.506
Sam and dean winchester, you
have the right to remain silent.

00:09:41.507 --> 00:09:44.550
Anything you say can and will be used
against you in a court of law.

00:09:44.551 --> 00:09:48.781
You have the right to speak to an attorney and
have an attorney present during any questioning.

00:09:48.782 --> 00:09:52.998
If you cannot afford a lawyer, one will be
appointed for you at government expense.

00:09:52.999 --> 00:09:54.240
Hi, guys.

00:09:56.406 --> 00:09:57.833
It's been a while.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:07.833
Supernatural 312
synchro : Flolo - Transcript: Yyets.Net

00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:17.532
- So, did you get them?
- Where is everyone? I asked for all your men.

00:10:17.533 --> 00:10:19.791
And you got them.
They went with you on the raid.

00:10:19.792 --> 00:10:21.339
Four men? That's all?

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.927
Everyone i could drum up
with an hour's notice.

00:10:23.928 --> 00:10:26.483
We're a small town, agent henriksen.

00:10:35.233 --> 00:10:37.624
- What's he in for?
- Drunk and disorderly.

00:10:37.625 --> 00:10:39.140
Keys.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.719
Now.

00:10:42.752 --> 00:10:44.815
What are you doing?

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.139
It is your lucky night, sir.
You are free to go.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.239
- What the hell are you doing?
- This way.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.772
Agent henriksen, you can't
just release my prisoners.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:59.039
Agent henriksen.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:02.727
- Look. I get it... you're may berry p.D.
- Excuse me?

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:04.867
And this isn't how i'd do it
if i had my choice,

00:11:04.868 --> 00:11:07.639
But a tip's a tip,
and we had to move fast.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.150
Look, agent, this ain't my first rodeo.

00:11:11.151 --> 00:11:14.103
You've never been
to a rodeo like this before.

00:11:14.104 --> 00:11:16.239
You have any idea who we're
about to bring in here?

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.640
Yeah... a couple of fugitives.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.239
The most dangerous criminals you've
ever laid your eyeballs on.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.296
Think hannibal lecter and his half-Wit little
brother. Do you know what these guys do for kicks?

00:11:24.297 --> 00:11:28.439
Dig up graves and mutilate corpses. They're not just killers,
sheriff. They're satan-Worshipping, nutbag killers.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.555
So work with me here. I'll get them out your hair
and on their way to supermax,

00:11:32.556 --> 00:11:36.217
And you'll be home
in enough time to watch the farm report.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.040
However we can help.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:43.340
Those men of yours...
post them at the exits.

00:11:44.244 --> 00:11:45.840
Yes, sir.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.939
Reidy, bring them in.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.540
I guess we're as ready
as we're gonna be.

00:12:12.357 --> 00:12:14.340
Why all the sourpusses?

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.994
I'll show you to the cells.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:22.035
Hey! Hey!
Watch the merchandise!

00:12:23.165 --> 00:12:25.740
We're not the ones
you should be scared of, nancy.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.440
Dean, come on!

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.239
All right.
All right.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.830
- Sit?
- Yeah.

00:12:56.525 --> 00:12:58.539
How we gonna
houdini out of this one?

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.320
Good question.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.470
It's me.
Steven in?

00:13:08.524 --> 00:13:10.685
Well, get him
out of the meeting.

00:13:17.648 --> 00:13:19.944
- Groves.
- I got them.

00:13:20.094 --> 00:13:22.138
Well, i'll be damned.

00:13:22.343 --> 00:13:26.064
I was betting on your headstone reading
"couldn't catch the winchester boys."

00:13:26.065 --> 00:13:28.639
- Well, they'll be at supermax by morning.
- How?

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.387
Armored bus, loaded with men.

00:13:30.388 --> 00:13:32.539
A bus? What, are you trying
to give me another ulcer?

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:36.633
- Look, we're taking every precaution.
- Like the last time? And the time before that?

00:13:36.634 --> 00:13:38.746
Screw that.
I'm sending a chopper.

00:13:38.747 --> 00:13:42.050
- Whatever you think is best.
- Damn right. And i'll be on it.

00:13:42.051 --> 00:13:47.187
I can't take you losing those boys again. They
have been a primary thorn in my ass for months.

00:13:47.188 --> 00:13:48.339
- So, victor...
- Yeah?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.040
Glue your eyeballs to them
till i get there.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.939
- There's a chopper on its way.
- But we don't have a helicopter pad.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:58.540
Then clear
the damn parking lot.

00:14:11.362 --> 00:14:13.725
You know
what i'm trying to decide?

00:14:13.726 --> 00:14:17.028
I don't know. What? Whether cialis will
help you with your little condition?

00:14:17.028 --> 00:14:19.440
What to have for dinner
tonight.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.739
Steak or lobster. What the hell.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.439
Surf and turf.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:29.328
I got a lot to celebrate. I mean, after all,
seeing you two in chains...

00:14:29.329 --> 00:14:32.139
You kinky son of a bitch.
We don't swing that way.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:33.740
Now, that's funny.

00:14:34.301 --> 00:14:37.418
You know, i wouldn't bust out
the melted butter just yet.

00:14:37.419 --> 00:14:39.239
Couldn't catch us
at the bank.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.840
Couldn't keep us in that jail.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.739
You're right. Screwed up.
I underestimated you.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.519
I didn't count on you
being that smart. But now i'm ready.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:54.539
- Yeah, ready to lose us again?
- Ready like a court order to keep you

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:58.939
In a supermaximum prison in nevada till trial. Ready
like isolation in a soundproof, windowless cell

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.839
So small that, between you and me...

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:03.403
Probably unconstitutional.

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.820
How's that for ready?

00:15:09.383 --> 00:15:11.141
Take a good look at sam.

00:15:11.142 --> 00:15:13.540
You two will never
see each other again.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.988
Where's that smug smile, dean?

00:15:17.989 --> 00:15:19.716
I want to see it.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:27.079
- You got the wrong guys.
- Oh, yeah. I forgot. You fight monsters.

00:15:27.152 --> 00:15:30.739
Sorry, dean. Truth is, your daddy brainwashed
you with all that devil talk

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.283
And no doubt touched you in a bad place.

00:15:33.284 --> 00:15:36.139
- That's all. That's reality.
- Why don't you shut your mouth?

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:40.739
Well, guess what. Life sucks. Get a helmet.
'Cause everybody's got a sob story,

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:43.826
But not everybody
becomes a killer.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:53.021
And now i have two less
to worry about.

00:15:57.306 --> 00:15:59.640
It's surf-And-Turf time.

00:16:13.092 --> 00:16:14.339
Steven.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.040
Gentlemen.

00:16:18.352 --> 00:16:19.814
What's all this?

00:16:19.815 --> 00:16:23.839
What can i say? The fbi
didn't invent bureaucracy. We perfected it.

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:27.239
- You want me to do all this now?
- Sorry. Now, victor.

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:30.740
I'm gonna go take a good,
long gander at our fugitives.

00:16:53.684 --> 00:16:55.487
Sam and dean winchester.

00:16:55.488 --> 00:16:58.337
I'm deputy director steven groves.

00:16:58.338 --> 00:17:00.914
This is a pleasure.

00:17:00.915 --> 00:17:04.001
- Well, glad one of us feels that way.
- I've been waiting a long time

00:17:04.003 --> 00:17:06.429
For you two to come out of the woodwork.

00:17:31.211 --> 00:17:35.425
Sorry. Got to cut this short.
It's gonna be a long night, fellas.

00:17:41.539 --> 00:17:43.640
What the hell
was that?

00:17:46.317 --> 00:17:48.822
- Put the gun down!
- Wait. Okay, wait.

00:17:48.823 --> 00:17:50.936
- He shot him!
- I didn't shoot him. I didn't shoot anyone.

00:17:50.937 --> 00:17:52.939
- He shot me!
- Get on your knees now!

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:56.394
Okay, okay, okay.
Don't shoot. Please. Look. Here. Here.

00:17:58.501 --> 00:18:02.800
We didn't shoot him. Check the body.
There's no blood. We did not kill him.

00:18:09.539 --> 00:18:12.539
- Vic, there's no bullet wound.
- He's probably been dead for months.

00:18:12.539 --> 00:18:14.660
- What did you do to him?
- We didn't do anything!

00:18:14.661 --> 00:18:17.545
- Talk, or i shoot.
- You won't believe us.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.434
He was possessed.

00:18:20.539 --> 00:18:22.240
Possessed? Right.

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:24.852
Fire up the chopper.
We're taking them out of here now.

00:18:24.853 --> 00:18:27.543
- Yeah. Do that.
- Bill?

00:18:29.849 --> 00:18:31.831
Bill, are you there?

00:19:13.039 --> 00:19:16.338
They're dead.
I think they're all dead.

00:19:18.039 --> 00:19:20.134
What the hell was that? Reidy?

00:19:20.485 --> 00:19:22.221
Reidy?!

00:19:23.794 --> 00:19:24.695
Reidy?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.649
What the hell was that?

00:19:40.546 --> 00:19:43.265
- Hello?
- My men. Agent henriksen?

00:19:43.266 --> 00:19:46.378
- What the hell's happening out there?
- I can't get a line. All the phones are out.

00:19:46.378 --> 00:19:48.640
Henriksen!
Four of my men!

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:53.258
The internet, my cell... it's all dead.
How can it all be dead?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:07.439
- That can't be good.
- Oh, my god.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.841
No. It's okay, it's okay, it's okay. We're
gonna go. We're gonna go... right now.

00:20:10.842 --> 00:20:13.423
Nobody's going anywhere.
Everybody, calm down.

00:20:13.423 --> 00:20:15.418
Your partner is out there!
My men are out there!

00:20:15.419 --> 00:20:18.149
I know. We go out there,
we're asking to die, too.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.893
- Don't you get it?
- Get what?

00:20:19.894 --> 00:20:22.338
They're out there, and they're coming
in here. This is a siege.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:26.639
So this might be a good time for you to
lock the doors and the windows, take a breath,

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:30.992
And maybe deal with this like trained
professionals with some sense in their heads.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:44.673
You okay?

00:20:47.039 --> 00:20:50.249
I wouldn't think so. Nancy, right?

00:20:50.646 --> 00:20:53.139
I'm gonna get you through this.
You got my word.

00:20:53.508 --> 00:20:54.970
You got that?

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.338
All right,
don't be such a wuss.

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:02.278
What's the plan?

00:21:02.469 --> 00:21:05.039
Kill everyone in the station, bust you two out?

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:07.910
- What the hell are you talking about?
- I'm talking about your psycho friends.

00:21:07.911 --> 00:21:09.798
I'm talking about a bloodbath.

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:13.751
Okay, i promise you, whoever's out
there is not here to help us.

00:21:13.751 --> 00:21:17.139
Look, you got to believe us. Everyone here
is in terrible danger.

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:19.637
Why don't you let us out of here
so we can save your asses?

00:21:19.637 --> 00:21:21.085
From what?

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:23.751
You gonna say "demons"?

00:21:23.751 --> 00:21:27.374
Don't you dare say "demons."

00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:29.490
Let me tell you something.

00:21:29.492 --> 00:21:31.740
You should be
a lot more scared of me.

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:37.483
How's the shoulder?

00:21:39.039 --> 00:21:40.847
It's awesome.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:44.439
I'll live.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.239
You know,
if we get out of here alive.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.414
So, you got a plan?

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:02.927
Uh, please. Please. We need your
help. It's... it's nancy. Nancy, right?

00:22:03.021 --> 00:22:06.059
Nancy, my... my brother's been shot.
He's... he's bleeding really bad.

00:22:06.061 --> 00:22:10.461
You think maybe you could get us
a towel? Please? Just one clean towel?

00:22:12.311 --> 00:22:15.030
Look. Look at us.
We're not the bad guys, i swear.

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:22.169
Nice try.

00:22:29.780 --> 00:22:31.229
Thank you.

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:36.579
It's okay.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:43.440
Thank you.

00:22:51.398 --> 00:22:52.940
Thanks.

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:00.039
Let her go!
Let her go!

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:04.940
You okay, nance?

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:11.344
Try something again,
get shot. And not in the arm.

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:19.347
What the hell was that?

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.239
We're like sitting ducks in here.

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:32.639
Yeah, i know.

00:23:32.981 --> 00:23:35.646
Would it kill these cops
to bring us a snack?!

00:23:35.646 --> 00:23:38.139
- How many you figure are out there?
- I don't know.

00:23:38.140 --> 00:23:42.047
However many there are, they could be possessing
anyone. Anyone could just walk right in.

00:23:42.048 --> 00:23:44.288
It's kind of wild, right?

00:23:44.396 --> 00:23:46.717
I mean, it's like
they're coming right for us.

00:23:46.854 --> 00:23:49.108
They've never done that before.

00:23:51.144 --> 00:23:53.535
It's like we got
a contract on us.

00:23:54.140 --> 00:23:56.139
Think it's because we're so awesome?

00:23:56.140 --> 00:23:58.856
I think it's 'cause we're so awesome.

00:24:03.594 --> 00:24:06.505
Well, howdy, there, sheriff.

00:24:12.534 --> 00:24:15.472
- Uh, sheriff?
- It's time to go, boys.

00:24:16.840 --> 00:24:19.626
Uh... you know what?

00:24:19.628 --> 00:24:22.434
We're just comfy right here.
But thank you.

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:24.340
What do you think
you're doing?

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:27.501
We're not just gonna sit around here and
wait to die. We're gonna make a run for it.

00:24:27.503 --> 00:24:30.608
- It's safer here.
- There's a swat facility in boulder.

00:24:30.608 --> 00:24:33.601
- We're not going anywhere.
- The hell we're not.

00:24:43.835 --> 00:24:45.340
Stay back!

00:24:53.539 --> 00:24:56.704
- Hurry up!
- It's too late.

00:24:56.704 --> 00:24:59.963
I already called them.
They're already coming.

00:25:25.240 --> 00:25:26.539
Is he...

00:25:26.639 --> 00:25:28.461
Is he dead?

00:25:31.039 --> 00:25:32.750
Henriksen.

00:25:32.751 --> 00:25:35.416
Hey.
Is that you in there?

00:25:49.003 --> 00:25:50.999
I shot the sheriff.

00:25:52.340 --> 00:25:54.570
But you didn't shoot the deputy.

00:26:00.530 --> 00:26:02.893
Five minutes ago,
i was fine, and then...

00:26:02.894 --> 00:26:05.739
Let me guess...
some nasty black smoke

00:26:05.740 --> 00:26:08.206
Jammed itself down your throat?

00:26:09.867 --> 00:26:12.108
You were possessed.

00:26:12.840 --> 00:26:14.340
Possessed like...

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:15.739
Possessed.

00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:18.505
That's what it feels like.
Now you know.

00:26:18.862 --> 00:26:21.340
I owe you the biggest
"i told you so" ever.

00:26:33.624 --> 00:26:35.539
Officer amici.

00:26:35.639 --> 00:26:37.541
Keys.

00:26:44.144 --> 00:26:45.771
All right.

00:26:45.771 --> 00:26:47.967
So, how do we survive?

00:27:05.652 --> 00:27:08.373
Well, that's nice.
It's not gonna do much good.

00:27:08.374 --> 00:27:12.253
- We got an arsenal here.
- You don't poke a bear with a bb gun.

00:27:12.253 --> 00:27:15.039
- That's just gonna make him mad.
- What do you need?

00:27:15.039 --> 00:27:17.239
- Salt. Lots and lots of salt.
- Salt?

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:19.593
What, is there an echo in here?

00:27:19.594 --> 00:27:21.938
There's road salt
in the storeroom.

00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:23.536
Perfect.

00:27:23.537 --> 00:27:26.847
Perfect. We need salt
at every window and every door.

00:27:32.340 --> 00:27:34.240
How you holding up,
nancy?

00:27:34.340 --> 00:27:36.046
Okay.

00:27:37.731 --> 00:27:39.672
When i was little,

00:27:39.673 --> 00:27:43.197
I would come home from church
and talk about the devil.

00:27:43.199 --> 00:27:46.139
My parents would tell me
to stop being so literal.

00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:50.539
I guess i showed them,
huh?

00:27:52.296 --> 00:27:53.867
That should hold.

00:27:53.867 --> 00:27:55.340
Thank you.

00:27:59.391 --> 00:28:01.539
Hey, where's my car?

00:28:01.539 --> 00:28:03.778
Impound lot out back.

00:28:03.780 --> 00:28:05.336
Wait.

00:28:05.338 --> 00:28:07.452
You're not
going out there?

00:28:08.063 --> 00:28:10.593
Yeah. I got to get something
out of my trunk.

00:29:25.840 --> 00:29:27.740
They're coming!

00:29:31.715 --> 00:29:33.440
Hurry!

00:30:24.639 --> 00:30:27.271
- Everybody okay?
- Define "okay."

00:30:27.273 --> 00:30:29.842
All right, everybody needs
to put these on.

00:30:29.843 --> 00:30:32.440
They'll keep you
from being possessed.

00:30:36.394 --> 00:30:38.690
What about you and sam?

00:30:41.639 --> 00:30:44.639
- Smart.
- How long you had those?

00:30:44.639 --> 00:30:46.730
Not long enough.

00:31:04.039 --> 00:31:06.280
Hey, that's jenna rubner.

00:31:09.139 --> 00:31:10.938
It's not jenna anymore.

00:31:10.940 --> 00:31:13.438
That's where all that
black demon smoke went?

00:31:13.440 --> 00:31:15.192
Looks like.

00:31:38.528 --> 00:31:41.041
Shotgun shells full of salt.

00:31:42.063 --> 00:31:46.244
- Whatever works.
- Fighting off monsters with condiments.

00:31:47.450 --> 00:31:50.784
So, turns out
demons are real.

00:31:52.182 --> 00:31:55.039
F.Y.I...
ghosts are real, too.

00:31:55.467 --> 00:31:59.539
So are werewolves,
vampires, changelings,

00:31:59.539 --> 00:32:01.875
Evil clowns that eat people.

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:04.414
Okay, then.

00:32:04.416 --> 00:32:06.891
If it makes you feel better,
bigfoot's a hoax.

00:32:07.840 --> 00:32:09.579
It doesn't.

00:32:11.340 --> 00:32:12.992
How many demons?

00:32:12.992 --> 00:32:14.438
Total?

00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:15.940
No clue.

00:32:16.039 --> 00:32:17.979
A lot.

00:32:19.385 --> 00:32:21.653
You know what my job is?

00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:25.847
You mean besides
locking up the good guys?

00:32:26.340 --> 00:32:27.965
I have no idea.

00:32:28.240 --> 00:32:29.940
My job is boring.

00:32:30.039 --> 00:32:31.468
It's frustrating.

00:32:31.469 --> 00:32:33.938
You work three years for one break,

00:32:33.940 --> 00:32:37.739
And then maybe you can save...
a few people. Maybe.

00:32:38.188 --> 00:32:40.139
That's the payoff.

00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:42.239
I've been busting my ass for 15 years

00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:44.440
To nail a handful of guys,
and all this while,

00:32:44.539 --> 00:32:46.639
There was something
off in the corner so big.

00:32:46.740 --> 00:32:48.139
So, yeah.

00:32:48.139 --> 00:32:51.739
Sign me up for that big, frosty
mug of wasting my damn life.

00:32:51.740 --> 00:32:53.239
You didn't know.

00:32:53.240 --> 00:32:54.940
Now i do.

00:32:59.740 --> 00:33:01.519
What's out there?

00:33:01.831 --> 00:33:03.690
Can you guys beat it?

00:33:03.943 --> 00:33:05.550
Can you win?

00:33:07.858 --> 00:33:11.039
Honestly, i think
the world's gonna end bloody.

00:33:12.340 --> 00:33:14.311
But it doesn't mean
we shouldn't fight.

00:33:14.840 --> 00:33:16.239
We do have choices.

00:33:16.240 --> 00:33:18.469
I choose to go down swingin'.

00:33:22.039 --> 00:33:24.916
Plus, you got nothing
to go home to but your brother.

00:33:25.940 --> 00:33:27.056
Yeah.

00:33:28.722 --> 00:33:31.639
What about you? You rockin'
the white picket fence?

00:33:32.063 --> 00:33:34.843
Empty apartment,
string of angry ex-Wives.

00:33:35.436 --> 00:33:37.351
I'm right where you are.

00:33:39.940 --> 00:33:41.541
Imagine that.

00:33:46.610 --> 00:33:48.438
- How do we kill her?
- We don't.

00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:50.639
- She's a demon.
- She's here to help us.

00:33:50.639 --> 00:33:52.561
Are you kidding?

00:33:57.421 --> 00:33:59.266
Are you gonna let me out?

00:34:06.440 --> 00:34:08.840
And they say chivalry's dead.

00:34:09.909 --> 00:34:12.976
Does anyone have a breath mint?
Some guts splattered in my mouth

00:34:12.976 --> 00:34:15.724
While i was killing my way in here.

00:34:27.088 --> 00:34:31.539
- How many are out there?
- 30, at least. That's so far.

00:34:31.539 --> 00:34:34.838
Oh, good. 30.
30 hit men, all gunning for us.

00:34:34.840 --> 00:34:37.221
Who sent them?

00:34:38.329 --> 00:34:40.338
You didn't tell dean?

00:34:40.463 --> 00:34:42.239
I'm surprised.

00:34:42.240 --> 00:34:44.639
- Tell me what?
- There's a big new up-And-Comer.

00:34:44.639 --> 00:34:47.139
Real pied piper.

00:34:47.139 --> 00:34:49.438
- Who is he?
- Not he.

00:34:49.440 --> 00:34:51.137
Her.

00:34:51.139 --> 00:34:53.239
- Her name is lilith.
- Lilith?

00:34:53.240 --> 00:34:56.838
And she really, really wants
sam's intestines on a stick.

00:34:56.840 --> 00:34:59.639
'Cause she sees him as competition.

00:34:59.639 --> 00:35:01.465
You knew about this?

00:35:03.639 --> 00:35:06.494
Well, gee, sam, is there
anything else i should know?!

00:35:07.340 --> 00:35:09.838
How about the two of you
talk about this later?

00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:11.633
We'll need the colt.

00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:19.057
Where's the colt?

00:35:20.440 --> 00:35:23.539
- It got stolen.
- I'm sorry. I must have blood in my ear.

00:35:23.539 --> 00:35:26.039
I thought i just heard you say
that you were stupid enough

00:35:26.139 --> 00:35:29.936
To let the colt get grabbed out of
your thick, clumsy, idiotic hands.

00:35:31.639 --> 00:35:33.539
Fantastic.

00:35:34.414 --> 00:35:36.438
This is just peachy.

00:35:36.440 --> 00:35:38.340
- Ruby...
- Shut up.

00:35:41.639 --> 00:35:43.240
Fine.

00:35:45.358 --> 00:35:48.039
Since i don't see
that there's any other option,

00:35:48.139 --> 00:35:50.974
There's one other way i know how
to get you out of here alive.

00:35:51.074 --> 00:35:53.938
- What's that?
- I know a spell.

00:35:53.940 --> 00:35:57.807
It'll vaporize every demon
in a one-Mile radius...

00:35:57.807 --> 00:35:59.965
Myself included.

00:36:00.599 --> 00:36:04.588
So, you let the colt out of your sight,
and now i have to die.

00:36:05.345 --> 00:36:07.938
So, next time, be more careful.

00:36:07.940 --> 00:36:10.780
How's that for a dying wish?

00:36:14.148 --> 00:36:17.338
Okay.
What do we need to do?

00:36:17.514 --> 00:36:21.282
You can't do anything. This spell
is very specific.

00:36:21.340 --> 00:36:23.039
It calls
for a person of virtue.

00:36:24.340 --> 00:36:26.325
I got virtue.

00:36:26.701 --> 00:36:29.940
Nice try.
You're not a virgin.

00:36:31.039 --> 00:36:33.039
Nobody's a virgin.

00:36:44.215 --> 00:36:45.438
No.

00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:47.039
No way.

00:36:47.139 --> 00:36:50.695
- You're kidding me. You're...
- What? It's a choice, okay?

00:36:50.740 --> 00:36:53.338
So, y-You've never...

00:36:53.651 --> 00:36:55.340
Not even once?

00:36:55.440 --> 00:36:57.356
I mean, not even...

00:37:00.539 --> 00:37:02.938
So, this spell...

00:37:02.940 --> 00:37:04.639
What can i do?

00:37:04.639 --> 00:37:06.588
You can hold still.

00:37:07.322 --> 00:37:09.496
While i cut your heart
out of your chest.

00:37:09.497 --> 00:37:10.740
- What?
- What are you, crazy?

00:37:10.740 --> 00:37:13.626
- I'm offering a solution.
- You're offering to kill somebody.

00:37:13.628 --> 00:37:16.148
And what do you think's gonna happen to
this girl when the demons get in?

00:37:16.150 --> 00:37:18.438
- We're gonna protect her. That's what.
- Very noble.

00:37:18.440 --> 00:37:21.438
- Excuse me.
- You're all gonna die. Look, this is the only way.

00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:24.932
- Yeah, yeah. There's no way that you're gonna...
- Would everybody please shut up?!

00:37:25.940 --> 00:37:28.139
All the people out there...

00:37:28.139 --> 00:37:29.941
Will it save them?

00:37:29.942 --> 00:37:32.242
It'll blow the demons out of their bodies.

00:37:32.242 --> 00:37:35.556
So if their bodies
are okay... yeah.

00:37:42.077 --> 00:37:43.403
I'll do it.

00:37:43.405 --> 00:37:45.255
- No, no. You don't need to do this.
- Hell no!

00:37:45.255 --> 00:37:48.039
- All my friends are out there.
- We don't sacrifice people.

00:37:48.039 --> 00:37:50.829
We do that,
we're no better than them.

00:37:52.409 --> 00:37:54.269
We don't have a choice.

00:37:54.269 --> 00:37:58.224
- Yeah, well, your choice is not a choice.
- Sam, you know i'm right.

00:38:02.940 --> 00:38:04.039
Sam.

00:38:05.639 --> 00:38:07.838
What the hell is going on?
Sam, tell her.

00:38:09.034 --> 00:38:10.864
It's my decision.

00:38:10.865 --> 00:38:12.739
Damn straight, cherry pie.

00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:14.213
Stop!

00:38:14.213 --> 00:38:15.838
Stop!

00:38:15.840 --> 00:38:18.240
Nobody kill any virgins!

00:38:20.240 --> 00:38:22.840
Sam,
i need to talk to you.

00:38:27.604 --> 00:38:29.831
Please tell me you're not
actually considering this.

00:38:29.831 --> 00:38:31.840
We're talking about holding down a
girl and cutting out her heart.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.338
And we're also talking about
30 people out there, dean...

00:38:34.340 --> 00:38:38.115
Innocent people who are all gonna die,
along with everyone in here.

00:38:38.117 --> 00:38:41.811
It doesn't mean that we throw away the
rule book and stop acting like humans.

00:38:42.139 --> 00:38:45.563
I'm not gonna let that demon
kill some nice, sweet, innocent girl

00:38:45.563 --> 00:38:47.438
Who hasn't even been laid.

00:38:47.440 --> 00:38:50.139
I mean, look, if that's how you win
wars, then i don't want to win.

00:38:50.141 --> 00:38:52.740
Then what?
What do we do, dean?

00:38:58.378 --> 00:39:01.239
I got a plan. I'm not saying
it's a good one.

00:39:01.240 --> 00:39:04.539
I'm not even saying that it'll work.
But it sure as hell beats killing a virgin.

00:39:04.539 --> 00:39:06.340
Okay, so, what's the plan?

00:39:06.440 --> 00:39:09.340
Open the doors,
let them all in...

00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:11.313
And we fight.

00:39:17.840 --> 00:39:20.338
- Get the equipment to work?
- Yeah.

00:39:20.340 --> 00:39:22.543
- So?
- So, this is insane.

00:39:22.543 --> 00:39:25.197
You win "understatement of the year."
Look, i get it. You think...

00:39:25.197 --> 00:39:27.139
I don't think... i know.

00:39:27.139 --> 00:39:29.621
It's not gonna work.

00:39:30.440 --> 00:39:32.168
So long, boys.

00:39:32.170 --> 00:39:35.144
- So, you're just gonna leave?
- Hey.

00:39:35.440 --> 00:39:38.300
I was gonna kill myself
to help you win.

00:39:38.974 --> 00:39:41.681
I'm not gonna stand here
and watch you lose.

00:39:45.039 --> 00:39:48.039
And i'm disappointed...
because i tried.

00:39:48.139 --> 00:39:50.239
I really did.

00:39:50.592 --> 00:39:53.845
But, clearly,
i bet on the wrong horse.

00:39:58.340 --> 00:40:00.639
Do you mind letting me out?

00:40:16.639 --> 00:40:18.860
I'm leaving.

00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:21.755
Who wants to stop me?

00:40:39.980 --> 00:40:41.483
All set?!

00:40:41.485 --> 00:40:43.001
Yeah!

00:40:43.340 --> 00:40:45.340
Let's do this!

00:41:42.440 --> 00:41:44.625
God,
i hope this works.

00:41:59.012 --> 00:42:00.666
Go! Go! Go!

00:42:20.976 --> 00:42:24.610
When this is over,
i'm gonna have so much sex.

00:42:26.139 --> 00:42:27.929
But not with you.

00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:30.474
We better move.

00:43:36.621 --> 00:43:38.849
Henriksen, now!

00:45:34.340 --> 00:45:37.639
I better call in. Hell of a story
i won't be telling.

00:45:37.639 --> 00:45:39.713
So, what are you
gonna tell them?

00:45:39.715 --> 00:45:42.639
The least ridiculous lie i can come up
with in the next five minutes.

00:45:42.639 --> 00:45:45.538
Good luck with that. Not to pressure
you or anything,

00:45:45.539 --> 00:45:48.913
- But what are you planning to do about us?
- I'm gonna kill you.

00:45:49.539 --> 00:45:53.556
Sam and dean winchester were in the
chopper when it caught on fire.

00:45:53.557 --> 00:45:57.275
Nothing's left. Can't even identify them
with dental records.

00:45:58.961 --> 00:46:01.108
Rest in peace, guys.

00:46:11.739 --> 00:46:13.239
Now get out of here.

00:46:13.688 --> 00:46:15.039
Yeah.

00:46:31.940 --> 00:46:34.346
Oh. Hey, there.

00:46:34.346 --> 00:46:38.619
Excuse me. I'm looking for two boys.
They're brothers.

00:46:38.619 --> 00:46:41.739
One's really tall,
and one's really cute.

00:46:41.739 --> 00:46:43.898
What's your name,
sweetie?

00:46:45.054 --> 00:46:46.516
Lilith.

00:47:08.612 --> 00:47:10.525
Turn on the news.

00:47:13.039 --> 00:47:15.965
The community
is still reeling

00:47:15.965 --> 00:47:18.541
From the tragedy that happened
just a few hours ago.

00:47:18.543 --> 00:47:22.652
Authorities believe a gas main ruptured,
causing the massive explosion

00:47:22.652 --> 00:47:26.938
That ripped apart the police station
and claimed the lives of everyone inside.

00:47:26.940 --> 00:47:30.867
Among the deceased, at least
six police officers and staff,

00:47:30.869 --> 00:47:35.818
Including sheriff melvin dodd, deputy phil
amici, and secretary nancy fitzgerald,

00:47:35.820 --> 00:47:41.050
As well as three fbi agents, identified as
steven groves, calvin reidy, and victor henriksen.

00:47:41.050 --> 00:47:44.081
Two fugitives in custody were also killed.

00:47:44.083 --> 00:47:48.451
We'll continue to follow the story here
at the scene, but for now, back to you, jim.

00:47:55.842 --> 00:48:00.708
- Must have happened right after we left.
- Considering the size of the blast...

00:48:01.440 --> 00:48:03.838
... smart money's on lilith.

00:48:04.230 --> 00:48:06.976
- What's in these?
- Something that'll protect you,

00:48:06.978 --> 00:48:10.228
Throw lilith off your trail...
for the time being, at least.

00:48:10.230 --> 00:48:15.489
- Thanks.
- Don't thank me. Lilith killed everyone.

00:48:15.490 --> 00:48:19.938
She slaughtered your precious little
virgin, plus a half a dozen other people.

00:48:20.420 --> 00:48:23.447
So, after your big speech
about humanity and war,

00:48:23.447 --> 00:48:27.288
Turns out your plan
was the one with the body count.

00:48:27.766 --> 00:48:30.279
Do you know how to fight a battle?

00:48:30.280 --> 00:48:35.047
You strike fast, and you don't leave any survivors,
so no one can go running to tell the boss.

00:48:35.048 --> 00:48:38.465
So, next time... we go with my plan.

00:48:54.048 --> 00:48:58.465
